            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0776" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.936/12–1045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Robertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-10T18:00:00-05:00">December 10,
                            1945—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1966. Dept desires that Embassy extract from files and have ready for General
                    Marshall’s perusal on his arrival in Chungking telegrams, reports and other
                    documents relating to various recent important political, economic and military
                    developments and that Embassy prepare a statement of current problems that need
                    to be taken up with the Chinese authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
